% Twin of RefPausable (OpenZeppelin Contracts 5.0.2, utils/Pausable.sol with access/Ownable.sol), translated by InsurLE2/migration/solidity (sol_front.pl).
% One law per success path of each state-changing function, one integrity constraint per revert path;
% the reverts' reasons are the comments above the constraints. See pausable.ledger.md;
% the contract itself: sources/RefPausable.sol (Show the Original). Who may do what, when, with which effect: the Legal View command
% (Misc in either editor), computed from this program.
% It extends ownable (their twins' files are beside it): their laws, constraints and templates are its own,
% and what follows is what RefPausable adds to them.

the target language is: lps.

the knowledge base pausable reference model extends ownable.

the maximum time is 7.

the actions are:
    *a pauser* pauses the token; known as pause.
    *a pauser* unpauses the token; known as unpause.

the fluents are:
    the token is paused; known as paused.

the knowledge base pausable reference model includes:

initially the owner of the token is alice.

% pause
% reverts: OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
it must not be true that
    a pauser pauses the token
    and the owner of the token is an account
    and the account is different from the pauser.

% reverts: EnforcedPause
it must not be true that
    a pauser pauses the token
    and the token is paused.

when a pauser pauses the token
then the token is paused.

% unpause
% reverts: OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
it must not be true that
    a pauser unpauses the token
    and the owner of the token is an account
    and the account is different from the pauser.

% reverts: ExpectedPause
it must not be true that
    a pauser unpauses the token
    and it is not the case that the token is paused.

when a pauser unpauses the token
then it is not the case that the token is paused.

% The final state of the scenario below: what the EVM gives for the same calls, and what the twin's run
% under LPS2 reaches (checked by InsurLE2/migration/solidity/test_solidity.pl; the calls the scenario marks
% as reverted leave no trace):
%   - the owner of the token is alice
%   - the token is paused
% Run it: Misc > Run in LPS in the Logical English editor, or open it in the LPS2 IDE.
% Who may do what, as queries: Misc > Legal View (of This LPS Program), in either editor.
scenario one is:
    % the EVM reverts the next call (not the owner): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    bob pauses the token from 1 to 2.
    alice pauses the token from 2 to 3.
    % the EVM reverts the next call (EnforcedPause): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    alice pauses the token from 3 to 4.
    alice unpauses the token from 4 to 5.
    alice pauses the token from 5 to 6.

